  "abstract": {
    "value": "An electroreductive cross-coupling of prop-2-yn-1-yl acetates with chloro(vinyl)silanes for producing tetrasubstituted silylallenes is developed. The method enables the formation of a new C�Si bond through the cathodic reduction formation of the silyl radical, radical addition across the $\\mathrm { C } { \\equiv } \\mathrm { C }$ bond, the alkenyl anion intermediate formation, and deacetoxylation and represents a mild, practical route to the synthesis of silylallenes. Mechanistic studies reveal that $\\mathrm { C o C l } _ { 2 }$ acts as the mediator to promote the formation of the alkenyl anion intermediate via electron transfer.",
